  "label": "Camels are mapped as 'terrorists' in the text",
  "description": "The text at the bottom, '...they're re all terrorists', explicitly maps the visual entity 'shouting_camels' (the three camels) onto the concept of 'terrorists'. This is an analogical mapping where the camels, through their visual portrayal of shouting or roaring, are equated with terrorists, leveraging the stereotype that camels (as symbols of the Middle East) represent all Muslims or Middle Easterners who are terrorists. This mapping is central to the meme's hateful intent.",
